<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine grain futures market shifts session.</title>
<headline>Argentine grain futures market shifts session.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Buenos Aires Futures Market, Argentina's largest grains futures market, said Thursday it will open half an hour earlier as of next Monday in response to a seasonal adjustment of clocks in Chicago.</p>
<p>Trading will begin at 1230 local time (1530 GMT).</p>
<p>The market has also added an extra 15 minutes each to the maize and wheat sessions to take account of the quantity of business.</p>
<p>The sessions will operate according to the following schedule (local times):</p>
<p>* Maize 1230 to 1315.</p>
<p>* Wheat 1330 to 1415.</p>
<p>* Soybeans 1445 to 1515.</p>
<p>* Sunflower seed 1530 to 1600.</p>
<p>-- Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655</p>
